<!DOCTYPE html>
<html class="antialiased" lang="en" style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
    <title>Netflix Hidden Categories & Secret Codes - Coffee & Fun LLC</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Search every hidden Netflix category and secret genre code in one list, more than 1,900 of them, each linking straight to its page on Netflix." />
    <meta name="keywords" content="netflix hidden categories, netflix secret codes, netflix genres, netflix categories, streaming" />
    <meta name="author" content="Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />

    <!-- Canonical URL -->
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.coffeeandfun.com{{ page.url }}" />

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/images/brand/favicon.png" sizes="any" />

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Coffee & Fun" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Netflix Hidden Categories & Secret Codes - Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Search every hidden Netflix category and secret genre code in one list, more than 1,900 of them, each linking straight to its page on Netflix." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com{{ page.url }}" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/home.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Coffee & Fun card with the coffee cup logo and the tagline Crafting software, one brew at a time" />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />

    <!-- Twitter Card -->
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:site" content="@bycoffeeandfun" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Netflix Hidden Categories & Secret Codes - Coffee & Fun LLC" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Search every hidden Netflix category and secret genre code in one list, more than 1,900 of them, each linking straight to its page on Netflix." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.coffeeandfun.com/assets/images/social/pages/home.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="Coffee & Fun card with the coffee cup logo and the tagline Crafting software, one brew at a time" />

    <meta name="theme-color" content="#141414" />

    <!-- Structured Data -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "CollectionPage",
        "name": "Netflix Hidden Categories & Secret Codes",
        "description": "A searchable list of {{ netflixCatalog.totalText }} Netflix hidden category codes, each linking straight to its page on Netflix.",
        "url": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com{{ page.url }}",
        "isPartOf": {
          "@type": "WebSite",
          "name": "Coffee & Fun",
          "url": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/"
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@id": "https://www.coffeeandfun.com/#organization"
        }
      }
    </script>

    {% pageCss "netflix" %}
    {% include sketch-styles.liquid %}
{% include schema-org.liquid %}

    </head>

<body>
    <a href="#tool" class="skip">Skip to the search</a>

    <main class="wrap">

        <div class="topbar">
            <a href="/" class="home-link" aria-label="Back to coffeeandfun.com">
                <img src="/assets/images/brand/coffee-and-fun-logo.png" alt="" width="40" height="40" decoding="async" />
                <span class="tip" aria-hidden="true">Back to coffeeandfun.com</span>
            </a>
        </div>

        <header>
            <h1>Every hidden Netflix category, in one list</h1>
            <p class="lede">Netflix sorts its catalog into numbered micro-genres, most never appear in its menus, but each one has a page you can open directly. Search all {{ netflixCatalog.totalText }} codes below, then jump straight to any of them on Netflix.</p>
        </header>

        <!-- Live status for screen readers (copy feedback) -->
        <div class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" id="announce"></div>

        <div class="searchbar" id="tool">
            <label class="sr-only" for="code-search">Search the categories</label>
            <input type="search" id="code-search" class="search"
                   placeholder="Try horror, british, 1980s, or a code like 1365"
                   autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="result-count" />
            <div class="meta-row">
                <p class="count" id="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">Showing all {{ netflixCatalog.totalText }} categories</p>
                <button type="button" class="linkish" id="clear-search" hidden>Clear search</button>
            </div>
            <noscript><p class="count">Searching needs JavaScript, but the full list below works without it.</p></noscript>
        </div>

        <div class="chipbar" id="chipbar" role="group" aria-label="Popular filters">
            <span class="chip-label" aria-hidden="true">Popular</span>
            {%- for tag in netflixCatalog.popularTags %}
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-tag="{{ tag }}">{{ tag }}</button>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        <nav class="letters" id="letters" aria-label="Jump to a letter">
            {%- for group in netflixCatalog.groups %}
            <a href="#sec-{{ group.slug }}">{{ group.label }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
        </nav>

        <div class="empty" id="no-results" hidden>
            <p>No categories match <strong id="no-results-q"></strong>.</p>
            <button type="button" class="linkish" id="clear-search-2">Clear the search</button>
        </div>

        <div id="catalog">
            {%- for group in netflixCatalog.groups %}
            <section class="gsec" id="sec-{{ group.slug }}" aria-labelledby="h-{{ group.slug }}">
                <h2 id="h-{{ group.slug }}"><span class="sr-only">Categories starting with </span>{{ group.label }} <span class="gcount">{{ group.items | size }}<span class="sr-only"> categories</span></span></h2>
                <ul>
                    {%- for item in group.items %}
                    <li><a href="https://www.netflix.com/browse/genre/{{ item.id }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ item.name | escape }}</a><code>{{ item.id }}</code><button type="button" class="copy">Copy link</button></li>
                    {%- endfor %}
                </ul>
            </section>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        <p class="backtop"><a href="#tool">Back to the search &uarr;</a></p>

        <section class="about" aria-labelledby="h-about">
            <h2 id="h-about">What are Netflix&rsquo;s hidden category codes?</h2>
            <p>Behind the scenes, Netflix files everything into thousands of oddly specific micro-genres, <strong>&ldquo;Cult Sci-Fi &amp; Fantasy from the 1970s&rdquo;</strong>, say, or <strong>&ldquo;Goofy Detective Movies&rdquo;</strong>. Each one has a number, and adding that number to <code>netflix.com/browse/genre/</code> opens its page, even when Netflix never shows you that shelf in its own menus.</p>

            <h2>How to use a code</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Search or browse</strong>, filter by genre, decade, country, mood, or an actor&rsquo;s name.</li>
                <li><strong>Open it on Netflix</strong>, every category links straight to its page. You&rsquo;ll need to be signed in to your own Netflix account.</li>
                <li><strong>Copy the link</strong>, save it or send it to someone so they land on the exact same shelf.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Good to know</h2>
            <p>Netflix&rsquo;s catalog differs by country, so a category can be full in one place and nearly empty in another. Codes also shuffle over time as Netflix reorganizes, if one comes up empty, try a search here for something similar.</p>
        </section>

        <p class="foot">The search happens in your browser, nothing you type leaves this page. Coffee &amp; Fun is not affiliated with Netflix, Inc.</p>
    </main>

    {% include footer.liquid %}

    {% pageJs "netflix" %}
</body>
</html>
